A||||10||BOILERMAKER||What type of gages for Turbo ||||1||
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||07-17-2001||06:55 PM||||I realize for a turbo setup one should have a Pyrometer and Boost gage.  Is there anything else???<P>What type of gages (mfr) are recommended?  Have any prices or part #'s?  I've also seen A-pillar gages.  Where should I look for these?||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||07-17-2001||06:59 PM||||Pyrometer, Boost/vac, and Air/fuel ratio!  Youll also need boost controller and a blow off valve!<P>added:  Check for all this in the Summit magazine!  Rice mag has nice gauges even though there is no difference!  As for a pillar mount a Integra one is what you gotta use but not sure from what year!<P>------------------<BR>      <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT><BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">         <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B><p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||07-17-2001||07:02 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BOILERMAKER:<BR><B>What type of gages (mfr) are recommended?  Have any prices or part #'s?  I've also seen A-pillar gages.  Where should I look for these?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Store</A> has an A-pillar gage mounting that allows you to mount two 2 <sup>1</sup>/<sub>16</sub>" gages to the A-pillar (gages not included) for $27.95.<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||BOILERMAKER||07-17-2001||09:48 PM||||On Summit's net page, I see that there are a couple of gauges.  Will the 10' long pyrometer cable be enough length?  Where would I route the cable?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||07-17-2001||10:42 PM||||All depends on where you run the cable.. 10' may or may not do it. I would get some cheap speaker wire and run it how you want to runthe cable and measure it...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||07-17-2001||11:40 PM||||You may also want an oil temp gauge (for 150 mph runs across the wasteland), and possibly and inlet air temp guage or some kind of knock sensor/light arrangement and possibly an ECM with a knock sensor input. That way the ECM retards timing when it detects knock, and you get a light on your dash to tell you this is going on and to get the Hell off the throttle.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||07-17-2001||11:40 PM||||You may also want an oil temp gauge (for 150 mph runs across the wasteland), and possibly and inlet air temp guage or some kind of knock sensor/light arrangement and possibly an ECM with a knock sensor input. That way the ECM retards timing when it detects knock, and you get a light on your dash to tell you this is going on and to get the Hell off the throttle.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||BOILERMAKER||07-18-2001||07:54 PM||||Has anyone ran the pyrometer in their car?  The one I am looking at (Autometer) comes with an 8' cord, but I'm not sure if this is long enough.  I'd hate to spend so much money and not get the length that I need.<P>Also, did you run it through the middle console and up around the dash?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||07-18-2001||08:20 PM||||i just run a combination vacume/boost gauge on mine. only required a vacume hose to be t-ed into the intake.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BOILERMAKER||07-19-2001||08:24 AM||||Yeah, I'm not worried as much about the Boost gauge as I can find PLENTY of tubing if I need it.  I'm just worried about the pyrometer not being long enough.||||reg||1
